      "text": [
        " : سَأَلْتُ أَبَا عَبْدِ اَللَّهِ عَلَيْهِ اَلسَّلاَمُ فِي اَلرَّجُلِ يُسْلِمُ فِي غَيْرِ زَرْعٍ وَ لاَ نَخْلٍ قَالَ \"يُسَمِّي كَيْلاً مَعْلُوماً إِلَى أَجَلٍ مَعْلُومٍ\" قَالَ وَ سَأَلْتُهُ عَنِ اَلسَّلَمِ فِي اَلْحَيَوَانِ وَ اَلطَّعَامِ وَ يَرْتَهِنَ اَلرَّجُلُ بِمَالِهِ رَهْناً قَالَ \"نَعَمْ اِسْتَوْثِقْ مِنْ مَالِكَ\"."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.3936 - Safwan bin Yahya narrated from Abdullah bin Sinan, who said:\nI asked Abu Abdillah (as) about a man who makes a forward contract (salam) for something other than crops or dates.\nImam (as) said: \"He should specify a known measure and set a fixed time for delivery.\"\nI also asked Imam (as) about making a forward contract for livestock or food and whether the creditor can take collateral for his money.\nImam (as) said: \"Yes, secure your wealth properly.\""
        ]
      }
